  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), compute the mean of those differences (i.e., expected value), and prefer the lottery with the more favorable (less negative) mean difference. However, in the verbal report, the individual does not mention differences from a reference value, expected values, or any calculation involving mean differences. Instead, they justify their choice based on preferring a higher probability of loss (i.e., a higher chance of a negative outcome), which is a different reasoning principle. The individual’s justification centers on the probability of loss, not on the magnitude of the loss adjusted by probability. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the required components of the decision reason. There is no evidence that they considered differences from a reference value or evaluated mean differences. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
