  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero, since no sure outcome exists), then evaluate the weighted mean of these differences. The individual does not mention any reference value, nor do they compute or refer to differences from zero. Instead, they make a qualitative comparison based on probability and prize size, specifically favoring a 50% chance of a smaller sum over a 25% chance of a larger sum. This does not align with the rule of the decision reason, which involves calculating and comparing mean differences from zero. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The information considered (probability and prize size) is different from the required analysis (differences from reference value weighted by probabilities). The justification lacks any reference to the mean difference or the reference value. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
